From: dasher@netcom.com (Anton Sherwood)
Date: Tue, 5 Apr 1994 23:52:18 -0700
Subject: [#94-4-48] those darn lefties

I wrote
> [...] left anarchists are the ones who take offense at being
> offered employment.  

and Tim Goodwin replied [94-4-34]
> There may well be some left anarchists who take offence at being
> offered employment.  I know of many who would welcome employment
> _on their own terms_.  Your statement is again either simplistic
> or malicious.

My statement was too broad in one way and too narrow in another.
Various leftists say, in various ways (though perhaps not in 
so many words), that it is "coercion" or "exploitation" or 
"harassment" to make you an offer *that you would turn down*.  
It is exploitation, according to the lefties in 
alt.society.anarchy, to OFFER wages.  It is harassment, 
according to some of the more rabid feminists, to INVITE 
a woman out.  It is coercion, according to some naked apes 
I've known, to advertise goods for sale.

If we are permitted only to make offers that we know the other
would accept, how can we bargain?  We can't, of course: altruists
don't dicker.


